# Remove the unsupportable "any CLI agent" extensibility claim (DRAFT, operator approval required)
#
# *** APPLY ORDER: THIS PATCH APPLIES ON TOP OF README-P0-worktree-isolation-claim.patch. ***
# Both edit adjacent rows of the features table, so applied against bare HEAD this one
# conflicts. Order is: P0 first, then this. (Caught by stack-testing the full set; each
# patch verifies clean individually against HEAD, which is not sufficient.)
#
# Developer Advocate closed question 3f: adding a fifth agent requires writing Go and
# recompiling. internal/agent/agent.go:157-168 is a hardcoded switch over four types;
# internal/agenttypes/types.go:8-12 defines exactly claude/gemini/codex/pi (+terminal, a raw
# shell that GetAgent never returns). A tree-wide grep for
# custom_agent|customagent|user_defined|plugin|registerAgent returns NOTHING — no registry,
# no plugin interface, no config file, no UI form, no env var.
#
# Compounding it: the switch's `default:` arm means an unknown agent_type returns HTTP 200
# ok:true and SILENTLY STARTS CLAUDE (observed by the Dev Advocate). A user testing our
# advertised extensibility gets a real Claude session burning their tokens and no error.
#
# Three claims imply user-facing extensibility that does not exist:
#   :37  "...or any CLI-based agent"
#   :81  "Any CLI-based agent can be added."
#   :110 "Any CLI agent | ...and any CLI-based tool"
#   :131 comparison table: "| Works with any CLI agent | ✓ | — | — | — | — |"
#
# *** REVISED — the earlier version of this patch fixed only THREE of the four. ***
# :131 claims a DISPROVEN capability as an advantage over four NAMED competitors, which is
# the worst placement for a false claim: it invites a check against tools where the feature
# genuinely exists. Found by grepping the fully-patched README rather than trusting the
# enumeration in this header. Note the FTS row was removed from this same table, four lines
# below, in a separate patch — I was editing this table and left another false row in it.
# (If the comparison table is deleted wholesale per the Strategist, this hunk is redundant.)
#
# The features row is retitled to carry the real differentiator (mixing vendors in one team,
# per the Strategist's wedge) rather than leaving a deflated cell behind. The requirements
# line additionally now states agents must be INSTALLED AND AUTHENTICATED — per the Dev
# Advocate, that is the real long pole on a clean machine and Coral does neither.
